---
/**
 * Field note: "Gen AI without data is a house on stilts"
 * → /field-notes/gen-ai-without-data/
 *
 * Its own look, and deliberately neither of the other two bare notes: a
 * harbour cutaway. The page is split by a waterline that runs through every
 * section, sky above and dark water below, with Archivo Black caption type
 * borrowed from the meme it opens with.
 *
 * The hero drawing is original work, drawn here in SVG rather than borrowed
 * from the circulating "AI FIRST / DATA FIRST" meme, whose author is unknown.
 * Same joke, our own pencil.
 *
 * Inter is already loaded site-wide (ThemeHead.astro); only Archivo and
 * Archivo Black are imported here.
 */
---

<div class="gnd">
  <div class="gnd-inner">
    <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
    <section class="gnd-hero">
      <p class="gnd-kicker">Field note &middot; AI and the semantic layer</p>
      <h1>&ldquo;AI first&rdquo; is a house on stilts.</h1>
      <p class="gnd-dek">
        Agentic workflows are a context problem. Everyone rents the same
        models. What differs between two teams is the quality of the ground
        they built on.
      </p>

      <!-- ============ THE DRAWING ============ -->
      <figure class="gnd-meme">
        <div class="gnd-panels">
          <!-- ---- panel A: AI first ---- -->
          <svg viewBox="0 0 260 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="gnd-a">
            <title id="gnd-a"
              >Cutaway of a large ornate building sitting above the waterline
              on thin crossed piles. Several piles are snapped and none of them
              reach the rock below.</title
            >
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="260" height="150" class="g-sky" />
            <rect x="0" y="150" width="260" height="180" class="g-water" />

            <!-- the building -->
            <g transform="rotate(-4 130 150)">
              <rect x="38" y="46" width="172" height="104" class="g-wall" />
              <rect x="146" y="18" width="64" height="30" class="g-wall" />
              <rect x="38" y="40" width="172" height="8" class="g-trim" />
